meta {
  name: Trigger Workflow
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/workflows/{{workflow_id}}/trigger
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "input_data": {
      "objet": "Entretien d embauche",
      "start_time": "2026-03-15T10:00:00.000Z",
      "attendee_name": "Julie Dupont",
      "attendee_email": "recruteur@entreprise-demo.fr"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Body must wrap params under "input_data" (WorkflowTriggerController reads
  body['input_data'], not top-level keys). Workflow.status must be "active"
  or this returns 400. Async: creates a WorkflowExecution (status: pending)
  and dispatches ExecuteWorkflowMessage -- poll "Get Workflow Execution" for
  the final status. Manual trigger -- conversation stays null on the
  resulting execution (only a tool call from a chat message sets it).

  Runs the real steps for real -- for THIS workflow that includes "Reserver
  sur Cal.eu" (see "Create Workflow Step (Cal.eu Booking)"), a real booking
  on Maxime's real Cal.eu account with a receivable email and a genuinely
  free ISO-8601 slot. Don't run with real attendee data unless you mean it.
}
